      When mounting an overhead storage rack to a garage ceiling, the fasteners are subjected to pure <strong>direct tensile withdrawal</strong> (pull-out force pulling straight down under gravitational acceleration). Unlike wall-mounted shelves where screws operate primarily in shear, ceiling screws must physically hold hundreds of pounds of suspended weight in wood grain tension. Here is the structural physics governing lag screw capacities and truss load limits.
    </p>

