        number: 1,
        title: "Counting Drywall Thickness as Wood Thread Embedment Depth",
        costImpact: "$1,600 (Under-Embedded Fasteners Pulling Free Under Load)",
        description: "A 3\" lag screw driven through 5/8\" drywall and a 1/8\" steel bracket leaves only 2-1/4\" of penetration into the wood joist.",
        solution: "Measure actual thread penetration into the solid wood member; ensure at least 2 to 2-1/2 inches of full thread bite into the timber framing."
      },
      {
        number: 2,
        title: "Overtorquing with a 1/2\" Pneumatic Impact Gun (Stripping Wood Threads)",
        costImpact: "$950 (Stripped Framing Holes & Adding Sistered Backer 2x4s)",
        description: "Hammering a lag screw until the wood fibers strip turns the pilot hole into smooth sawdust, destroying all withdrawal tensile strength.",
        solution: "Tighten lag screws until the steel washer draws firmly against the drywall face, then stop immediately. Finish tightening by hand with a ratchet."
